## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would thresholds vary by product area?
- How would you measure guardrail impact on velocity and reliability?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses planning, risk management, data integrity, and cross-team governance for a major migration; tests ability to define milestones, ownership, and metrics beyond high-level talk.

## Key Concepts

- Migration strategy and data integrity checks
- Downtime avoidance and phased rollout (canaries, dual-write)
- Rollback criteria, SLAs, and incident readiness
- Cross-team governance and staffing plans
- Metrics dashboards and validation artifacts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Basic idempotent migration hook (illustrative)
async function migrateBatch(batch) {
  for (const record of batch) {
    try {
      await writeToNewPlatform(record);
      await markAsMigrated(record.id);
    } catch (error) {
      await logMigrationError(record.id, error);
      // Continue processing other records
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical risk management when relying on external data and requires a concrete rollout plan across regions with resilience patterns and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and canary deployments
- SLOs and data freshness metrics
- Resilience patterns: circuit breakers, fallback caches
- Rollout artifacts, runbooks, and incident drills

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight circuit-breaker with fallback
class Breaker {
  constructor(threshold=3) { this.failures=0; this.open=false; }
  async call(fn) {
    if (this.open) throw new Error('Circuit open');
    try { return await fn(); } catch (e) { this.failures++; if (this.failures >= threshold) this.open=true; throw e; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate ETA accuracy during canary without impacting users?
- How would you design post-incident reviews and remedial actions?
